      "text": "Part 2 (20 Minutes)\nComplete Authentication Flow",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Part 2 (20 Minutes)\nComplete Authentication Flow",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ELxAWM7N7W-FTGs6M5olF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 831.8642903477696,
      "y": 7364.658171524046,
      "width": 1144,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 221909211,
      "version": 229,
      "versionNonce": 1435949307,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785474432881,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Imagine a brand new user.\n\nUser -> Clicks Signup -> Enter Name\n -> validate data -> Hash Password -> Store User -> Generate Verification Token -> Send Email -> success\n\n\nNotice:\nWe never store the actual password.\n\nWhy Not Store Plain Passwords?\n    Imagine our database is hacked.\n    If we stored:\n    amit@gmail.com\n    password123\n\nThe hacker immediately knows the password.\nInstead we store:\namit@gmail.com\n$2b$12$S9vXJ...\n\nThis is a hash.\nIt cannot be reversed.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Imagine a brand new user.\n\nUser -> Clicks Signup -> Enter Name\n -> validate data -> Hash Password -> Store User -> Generate Verification Token -> Send Email -> success\n\n\nNotice:\nWe never store the actual password.\n\nWhy Not Store Plain Passwords?\n    Imagine our database is hacked.\n    If we stored:\n    amit@gmail.com\n    password123\n\nThe hacker immediately knows the password.\nInstead we store:\namit@gmail.com\n$2b$12$S9vXJ...\n\nThis is a hash.\nIt cannot be reversed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FK4TyKa5f0DKVp0L3hR2U",
