      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "P-jAqih28tF4f-0wSS7ES",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 776.8642903477696,
      "y": 8251.306609024046,
      "width": 1386,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1487394197,
      "version": 253,
      "versionNonce": 1092845301,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785474886371,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "After login, how does the server remember the user?\nMany beginners answer: Database\nActually, for JWT, the server doesn't remember the login state.\nIt trusts the token.\n\nLogin Flow\n    User -> Login API -> Email + Password -> Backend -> Verify Password -> Generate JWT -> Return Token -> Client Stores Token\n\nThen every request becomes:\n    GET /projects\n    Authorization:\n    Bearer <JWT>\n\nBackend:\n    Receive JWT -> Verify Signature -> Extract User ID -> Load User -> Continue Request\n\nWhy JWT?\n    Without JWT:\n        Login ->  Server Stores Session -> Every Request ->  Lookup Session\n\n    With JWT:\n        Login -> Return Token -> Client Sends Token -> Server Verifies -> Done\n\nThis is why JWT is called stateless authentication.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "After login, how does the server remember the user?\nMany beginners answer: Database\nActually, for JWT, the server doesn't remember the login state.\nIt trusts the token.\n\nLogin Flow\n    User -> Login API -> Email + Password -> Backend -> Verify Password -> Generate JWT -> Return Token -> Client Stores Token\n\nThen every request becomes:\n    GET /projects\n    Authorization:\n    Bearer <JWT>\n\nBackend:\n    Receive JWT -> Verify Signature -> Extract User ID -> Load User -> Continue Request\n\nWhy JWT?\n    Without JWT:\n        Login ->  Server Stores Session -> Every Request ->  Lookup Session\n\n    With JWT:\n        Login -> Return Token -> Client Sends Token -> Server Verifies -> Done\n\nThis is why JWT is called stateless authentication.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
